# Tool-X

Tool-X is a practical, multi-platform development environment bootstrapper for Linux, macOS, and Windows.

It is designed to install the tools most developers need in a single pass: language runtimes, developer utilities, cloud CLIs, security tools, DevOps tooling, AI/ML dependencies, and Web3 tools.

## What Tool-X does

Tool-X helps you bring up a working development environment with a consistent structure:

- base system packages
- language runtimes
- compiler and runtime support
- CLI tools and libraries
- cloud tooling
- DevOps utilities
- AI/ML libraries
- Web3 tooling
- a unified `toolx` launcher

## Supported platforms

- Ubuntu / Debian Linux
- macOS
- Windows (via Git Bash, WSL, or shell environments)

## Important design note

This project is intentionally Linux-first. Linux is the primary target because it is the most predictable environment for package-based provisioning, automation, and repeatable installs.

macOS and Windows support are included as optional platform modules, but the most reliable path is Linux.

## Quick start

### Linux

```bash
git clone https://github.com/dannywise093-crypto/Tool-X.git
cd Tool-X
chmod +x setup.sh
./setup.sh
```

### macOS

```bash
git clone https://github.com/dannywise093-crypto/Tool-X.git
cd Tool-X
chmod +x setup.sh
./setup.sh
```

### Windows

Use Git Bash or WSL:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/dannywise093-crypto/Tool-X.git
cd Tool-X
chmod +x setup.sh
./setup.sh
```

## Commands

```bash
./setup.sh --help
./setup.sh --check
